description:
What: Add text filter to JMAP Email/query handler in crates/mail/src/email/query.rs.

Note: RFC 8621 §4.4.1 does not define a standard text property. We add an extension property named 'text' (matches headers + body per RFC spirit) following RFC 8621's extensibility rules.

Algorithm:
1. In crates/mail/src/email/query.rs, add parameter search_index: Option<&Arc<TantivySearchIndex>> to handle_email_query(). This requires making the function async.
   New signature:
   pub async fn handle_email_query(
       entries: &[EmailOverviewEntry],
       filter: Option<&serde_json::Value>,
       position: u64,
       limit: Option<u64>,
       state: &str,
       search_index: Option<&Arc<TantivySearchIndex>>,
   ) -> serde_json::Value

2. In the filter handling block, after existing filters (after, before, from, subject), add:
   if let Some(text_val) = filter.get("text").and_then(|v| v.as_str()) {
       if let Some(idx) = search_index {
           // query all groups for this text
           let cid_set: std::collections::HashSet<String> = ...;
           // For each article in entries, keep if its cid (as string) is in cid_set
           // OR if search is unavailable, skip filter (don't reject results)
           match idx.search_all_groups(text_val, 50000, 4096).await {
               Ok(cids) => {
                   let cid_set: HashSet<_> = cids.into_iter().collect();
                   entries_filtered.retain(|e| cid_set.contains(&e.cid.to_string()));
               }
               Err(_) => { /* search unavailable — return unfiltered rather than error */ }
           }
       } else {
           // search not configured; return empty list with an informative state
           // Alternatively: ignore the filter (behavior choice: ignore = less surprising)
       }
   }

3. Add search_all_groups method to TantivySearchIndex (or use search_in_group with empty group):
   pub async fn search_all(query: &str, max: usize, max_query_len: usize) -> Result<Vec<String>, SearchError>
   Returns Vec<String> of message_ids (stored field).

4. Update call sites in crates/mail/src/server.rs to pass search_index:
   handle_email_query(&entries, filter, 0, None, &state, jmap.search_index.as_ref().map(|x| x.as_ref())).await

5. Update JmapStores in crates/mail/src/server.rs or similar to include:
   pub search_index: Option<Arc<TantivySearchIndex>>,
   Wire it in from main config at startup.

Defensive rules: If search_index is None, ignore 'text' filter (return all results for other filters). Never panic. Never log text filter value. 'text' with empty string → return no filter change (all results).
